y if chosen carefully. In this setting, the optimal choice for ht is the marginal log-likelihood ahead \u2211T t log p(Ot:T |st, at),\nwhich is typically intractable to compute but can be approximated. In the context of avoiding collisions, this term estimates the likelihood of future collisions from a given state. A typical application of such heuristic factors in RLAI, as given by Piche\u0301 et al. (2019), is shown in Figure 2b."
